findings.detail:
1,050 transcript files in 5 folders, 23,046 tool calls.

Reads by target:
- product code 169, in 28 transcripts;
- repo docs 25;
- docs/program 600;
- other in repo 132;
- outside the repo 1,541.

Grep calls on code: 102. Bash searches: 6,792.

Search-then-read pairs (a search whose result names a file read within the next 6 calls): 181, of which 139 are distinct.
- The opened file is in docs/program 106 times, other in repo 48, code 26, repo docs 2.

Opened is not the same as needed. docs/program is untracked, so the corpus cannot be rebuilt as it stood at session time. These tasks are descriptive only.

LocAgent builds a graph with 4 node types (directory, file, class, function) and 4 edge types (contain, import, invoke, inherit). Its TraverseGraph tool takes start entities, direction, hops, entity types and relation types, and returns a tree.

Function Acc@10 (fine-tuned Qwen-2.5-7B):
- full system 71.53;
- hops fixed at 1: 66.79;
- without TraverseGraph: 66.06;
- contain edges only: 66.42;
- without SearchEntity: 53.28;
- without BM25: 60.22.

Acc@k requires all ground-truth locations to appear in the top k. Loc-Bench was built to avoid contamination.

A6-10 rules:
- sealed references, SHA-verified (97 quotes);
- 3 arms, 2 runs per arm per case, 30 runs in all, fresh workers;
- an equal budget of 16,000 tokens of tool-result material (chars/4) and 30 calls per run;
- a blinded evaluator scoring weighted obligations;
- a mechanical citation check;
- 'better' needs a 0.10 mean difference in the same direction in at least 4 of 5 cases;
- fewer tokens with a missing prerequisite is not a win;
- development cases are not holdouts.

The runs/ folder is empty.

The fit review later added:
- a no-history clone cut at the frozen commit;
- a key held back until after judging;
- a read log proving nothing past the freeze was opened;
- a 'not comparable' label for arms with different inputs.

recommendations_for_the_test:
Secondary metrics:
- recall at 2k, 4k and 16k tokens, plus file-hit recall;
- token precision;
- tokens to reach 80 % and 100 % recall;
- scripted lookups to 80 % recall (convertible to model steps at 6.6 s each);
- MRR and nDCG@10;
- value per token: area under the recall-vs-tokens curve from 0 to 16k;
- prerequisite loss on T3 and T4;
- build time, incremental update time, p50/p95 latency cold and warm, bytes on disk, RAM.

Sweep on the tune split only:
- hops 1-5 and PPR alpha 0.5, 0.7, 0.85;
- edge-type sets added cumulatively;
- ranking: BFS, degree-normalised, PPR, co-change weight, BM25, hybrid;
- granularity: file, symbol, chunk.
Report the full hop curve, not just the best point.

'Tuned on both sides' means:
- the same facts for both arms;
- the same number of configurations tried on the tune split;
- each engine's idiomatic indexes and settings (SQLite: indexes, ANALYZE, WAL, FTS5 with recursive CTEs; graph engine: id indexes and its library algorithms);
- the same packaging and tokenizer;
- no per-task rules.

Leakage controls:
- build every store at the parent commit, with history from ancestors only;
- drop same-PR sibling commits from co-change (primary), and report with siblings kept as secondary;
- exclude files added in the test commit, and commits with more than 30 files;
- never put the commit message in the query;
- for T3 and T4, build before the doc's commit and remove the doc;
- run a read-log audit.

Statistics:
- the unit is the commit, paired across arms, with PR clusters;
- 10k-resample cluster-bootstrap 95 % CIs and sign-flip permutation p-values; no CLT intervals;
- TOST with a smallest effect of interest of ±0.05;
- Holm correction for secondary metrics;
- report the realised paired SD.

Steps that need a model in the loop:
- annotate needed-but-unchanged context on 30-50 held-out commits (ContextBench style, with a human audit);
- blind real-task replays under the A6-10 budget (16k tool-result tokens, 30 calls, 2 or more runs per arm), each arm as the only retrieval tool, scored against sealed keys;
- any rewriting of commit subjects into task statements written as if before the fix.
